   The Simulation Setup Agent receives the cleaned protein and ligand PDBs from the Preprocessing Agent. It will first generate ligand topology parameters by invoking `generate_ligand_parameters` on `q13418_ATP_clean.pdb`. The resulting AMBER GAFF/GAFF2 parameters will be written to `q13418_ATP.itp` in the same directory.  

   Because the ligand atom names may not match the AMBER naming convention, the agent will run `map_ligand_atom_names` to produce a renamed ligand PDB (`q13418_ATP_mapped.pdb`) that aligns with the topology file.  

   With the protein PDB (`q13418_protein_clean.pdb`) and the mapped ligand PDB and its topology now available, the agent will call `build_simulation_system` with `protein_file` set to the cleaned protein and `output_dir` set to the current working directory. This tool orchestrates the creation of a GROMACS topology (`q13418_ATP.top`), a coordinate file in GRO format (`q13418_ATP.gro`), the standard TIP3P water box with a 1.2 nm cubic buffer, the addition of 0.15 M NaCl, and the generation of a default production MD parameter file (`production.mdp`) and a TPR file (`q13418_ATP.tpr`).  

   To satisfy the requirement of two independent 200 ns production replicas, the agent will duplicate the MD parameter file, creating `production_replica1.mdp` and `production_replica2.mdp`. It will edit each file to set a distinct `gen_seed` value (for example, 12345 for replica 1 and 67890 for replica 2). Correspondingly, it will generate two TPR files, `q13418_ATP_replica1.tpr` and `q13418_ATP_replica2.tpr`, by rerunning `build_simulation_system` or by invoking the internal TPR generator with the modified MD parameter files.  

   All generated files—including the ligand topology, the protein topology, the GRO coordinate file, the two MD parameter files, the two TPR files, and the pocket mapping JSON—will be written into the system directory `/home/akp66103/workspace/agenticAI/campaigns/robustness/campaigns/pseudokin_5x2/run_01/q13418_ATP/`. The Simulation Setup Agent will then terminate, having produced a complete, solvated, ion‑neutralized simulation system ready for production runs.
